# Never commit real keys. Set these in Netlify > Site configuration > Environment variables.

# ── Contact form ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without at least one delivery channel the form reports a real failure instead
# of pretending to send, and the visitor gets a mailto with their message
# already in it. Two channels, either one is enough:
#
#   1. Resend — set RESEND_API_KEY below (resend.com, free tier is 3,000/month),
#      then redeploy. This is the one that actually emails you.
#
#   2. Netlify Forms — no key, and confirmed working in production: a POST to
#      /__forms.html comes back with Netlify's "Thank you!" page, so every
#      submission is archived under Forms > contact. It depends on two things
#      that are easy to miss — Site configuration > Forms > form detection must
#      be ON, and a deploy has to run *after* it is switched on so the parser
#      gets a chance to read public/__forms.html. Archiving is not emailing:
#      add a notification under Forms > Notifications to get the message
#      in your inbox.
#
# Resend's shared sender only delivers to the address on the Resend account.
# To send from your own domain, verify romankucheryavyy.com in Resend and set
# CONTACT_FROM to something like "Portfolio <hello@romankucheryavyy.com>".
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_key_here
CONTACT_TO=kucheryavyyroman@gmail.com
CONTACT_FROM=Portfolio <onboarding@resend.dev>

# URL and DEPLOY_PRIME_URL are not set here: Netlify provides them at runtime,
# and the Netlify Forms channel only runs when one of them exists. Leave them
# unset locally, or the contact route will post to that origin.

# ── Resume ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlocks the /resume builder. Without it every PIN is refused.
RESUME_PIN=your-pin-here

# Claude, for the builder's tailor and cover-letter tools
# (/api/resume/tailor, /api/resume/cover-letter). Without it both answer
# "AI is not configured on the server". Each call bills this account.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here

# ── Build stamp (set by Netlify; nothing to fill in) ──────────────────────────
# COMMIT_REF and CONTEXT become BUILD_SHA and BUILD_CONTEXT in next.config.ts.
# Without them the stamp reads as a local build.
